#@testray.main.component.name = "Support QA"
#@type = "zendesk.frontend"

Feature: Zendesk Large File Attachment Employee Permissions
	Testing the large file uploader employee permissions.

Setup:
	* I get all test passwords and admin emails

Teardown:
	* I get the ID of the default user belonging to the organization "Lfazen - ${staticProjectName}" from zendesk.liferay.com
	* I teardown tickets requested by the users with the following email addresses from zendesk.liferay.com
	| lfa.customer1@lrcustomer.com.broken |
	* I tear down the accounts on koroneiki with the following names
	| Lfazen - ${staticProjectName} |
	* I tear down the accounts on koroneiki with the following "Code" values
	| LFAZENLFAZEN |
	* I synchronize the account entitlement definition with the name "Gold Subscription"
	* I tear down the projects with the following project codes via groovy
	| LFAZENLFAZEN |
	* I tear down the users with the following email addresses from okta
	| lfa.customer1@lrcustomer.com.broken |
	| lfa.employee1@liferay.com.broken    |
	| lfa.employee2@liferay.com.broken    |
	* I tear down the users with the following email addresses from customer.liferay.com
	| lfa.customer1@lrcustomer.com.broken |
	| lfa.employee1@liferay.com.broken    |
	| lfa.employee2@liferay.com.broken    |
	* I tear down the users with the following email addresses from koroneiki
	| lfa.customer1@lrcustomer.com.broken |
	| lfa.employee1@liferay.com.broken    |
	| lfa.employee2@liferay.com.broken    |
	* I tear down the contacts on koroneiki with the following email addresses
	| lfa.customer1@lrcustomer.com.broken |
	| lfa.employee1@liferay.com.broken    |
	| lfa.employee2@liferay.com.broken    |
	* I obtain the IDs of the following user email addresses from zendesk.liferay.com
	| lfa.customer1@lrcustomer.com.broken |
	| lfa.employee1@liferay.com.broken    |
	| lfa.employee2@liferay.com.broken    |
	* I teardown users with the following userIds "${staticUserIdList}" from zendesk.liferay.com
	* I obtain the external IDs of the following organizations from zendesk.liferay.com if still present
	| Lfazen - ${staticProjectName} |
	* I teardown organizations with the following organizationExternalIds "${staticOrganizationExternalIdList}" from zendesk.liferay.com
	* I teardown the user with userId "${staticDefaultUserId}" from zendesk.liferay.com

Scenario: View US data access file as employees
	@ help.center.acceptance = "true"
	Only employees with data access US permissions should be able to view links to large attachments to a ticket uploaded by a customer in the US region

	Given I generate a provisioning project name
	And I create a user with the following parameters
	| Screen Name   | lfa.customer1                       |
	| Email Address | lfa.customer1@lrcustomer.com.broken |
	| First Name    | LFA                                 |
	| Last Name     | Customer1                           |
	And I create a user with the following parameters
	| Screen Name   | lfa.employee1                    |
	| Email Address | lfa.employee1@liferay.com.broken |
	| First Name    | LFA                              |
	| Last Name     | Employee1                        |
	| Group         | Employees                        |
	And I create a user with the following parameters
	| Screen Name   | lfa.employee2                    |
	| Email Address | lfa.employee2@liferay.com.broken |
	| First Name    | LFA                              |
	| Last Name     | Employee2                        |
	| Group         | Employees                        |
	And I create an account on koroneiki with the following values
	| Code        | LFAZENLFAZEN                  | |
	| Data Region | United States                 | |
	| Language    | English                       | |
	| Name        | Lfazen - ${staticProjectName} | |
	| Region      | United States                 | |
	| Status      | Active                        | |
	| Tier        | T1                            | |
	And I assign the contact with the email address "lfa.customer1@lrcustomer.com.broken" on the account "Lfazen - ${staticProjectName}" to the following roles
	| Support Requester |
	And I generate static start and end dates
	And I create a product purchase for an account with the name "Lfazen - ${staticProjectName}" and the product "Portal Production" on koroneiki with the following values
	| End Date                | ${staticEndDate}         |   |
	| Original End Date       | ${staticOriginalEndDate} |   |
	| Perpetual               | false                    |   |
	| Product Field and Value | sizing                   | 1 |
	| Product Field and Value | licenses                 | 1 |
	| Product Field and Value | version                  | 6 |
	| Quantity                | 1                        |   |
	| Start Date              | ${staticStartDate}       |   |
	| Status                  | Approved                 |   |
	And I create a product purchase for an account with the name "Lfazen - ${staticProjectName}" and the product "Gold Subscription" on koroneiki with the following values
	| End Date                | ${staticEndDate}         | |
	| Original End Date       | ${staticOriginalEndDate} | |
	| Perpetual               | false                    | |
	| Quantity                | 1                        | |
	| Start Date              | ${staticStartDate}       | |
	| Status                  | Approved                 | |
	And I synchronize the account entitlement definition with the name "Gold Subscription"
	And I synchronize the contact entitlement definition with the name "Customer"
	And I synchronize the contact entitlement definition with the name "Customer - DXP"
	And I synchronize the contact entitlement definition with the name "Customer - Portal"
	And I synchronize the contact entitlement definition with the name "Customer - Commerce"
	And I synchronize the contact entitlement definition with the name "Liferay Employee"
	And I wait for "1" minutes
	Then the support organization with the code "LFAZENLFAZEN" should be part of the support site
	And the organization "Lfazen - ${staticProjectName}" should be present on zendesk.liferay.com
	And the support user with the email address "lfa.customer1@lrcustomer.com.broken" should be synced to the support site
	And the support user with the email address "lfa.employee1@liferay.com.broken" should be synced to the support site
	And the support user with the email address "lfa.employee2@liferay.com.broken" should be synced to the support site
	And the user with the email address "lfa.customer1@lrcustomer.com.broken" should be present on zendesk.liferay.com
	And the user with the email address "lfa.employee1@liferay.com.broken" should be present on zendesk.liferay.com
	And the user with the email address "lfa.employee2@liferay.com.broken" should be present on zendesk.liferay.com
	When I update the support password for user with the email address "lfa.customer1@lrcustomer.com.broken" to "${staticSupportUserTestPassword}"
	And I update the support password for user with the email address "lfa.employee1@liferay.com.broken" to "${staticSupportUserTestPassword}"
	And I update the support password for user with the email address "lfa.employee2@liferay.com.broken" to "${staticSupportUserTestPassword}"
	And I assign the support user with the email address "lfa.employee1@liferay.com.broken" to the support organization "Data Access US"
	And I assign the support user with the email address "lfa.employee2@liferay.com.broken" to the support organization "Data Access EU"
	When I update the user with the email address "lfa.customer1@lrcustomer.com.broken" to use the password "zendeskqauser"
	And I log out and log into the support homepage as "lfa.customer1@lrcustomer.com.broken" with password "${staticSupportUserTestPassword}"
	And I log into zendesk as "lfa.customer1@lrcustomer.com.broken" with password "zendeskqauser"
	And I create a request with the following values
	| Product       | Liferay Portal                          | 6.2                                   |
	| Component     | Activation Key & Project Administration |                                       |
	| System Status | Production                              | Functioning with limited capabilities |
	| Subject       | Request Subject                         |                                       |
	| Description   | Request Description                     |                                       |
	| Attachments   | Document_1.txt                          |                                       |
	Then I should be able to view a request with the following details
	| Subject       | Request Subject                                    |
	| Status        | OPEN                                               |
	| Requester     | LFA Customer1                                      |
	| Priority      | Normal                                             |
	| Product       | Liferay Portal > 6.2                               |
	| Sub-Status    | —                                                  |
	| Component     | Activation Key & Project Administration            |
	| System Status | Production > Functioning with limited capabilities |
	| Attachments   | Document_1.txt                                     |
	And I upload a file using the large file uploader with the following parameters
	| Attachment       | Document_2.txt      |
	| Comment          | Large File Comment  |
	| Data Region      | United States       |
	| No Personal Data | false               |
	Then I should be able to view a large file comment containing the text "Large File Comment" with the following details
	| Author      | LFA Customer1      |
	| Comment     | Large File Comment |
	| Attachment  | Document_2.txt     |
	When I log out and log into the support homepage as "lfa.employee1@liferay.com.broken" with password "${staticSupportUserTestPassword}"
	And I go to the Project Details page
	And I search for the project with the name "Lfazen - ${staticProjectName}"
	And I go to the project with the name "Lfazen - ${staticProjectName}"
	And I go to the Attachments tab
	Then the attachment with the keyword "Document_2.txt" should be visible with the following values
	| Ticket                         | ${staticRequestId} |
	| File Name                      | Document_2.txt     |
	| File Name Link                 | true               |
	| File Size                      | 1KB                |
	| Attached                       | LFA Customer1      |
	| Does Not Contain Personal Data | false              |
	And the attachment with the keyword "Document_2.txt" should not have the actions or delete link visible
	When I log out and log into the support homepage as "lfa.employee2@liferay.com.broken" with password "${staticSupportUserTestPassword}"
	And I go to the Project Details page
	And I search for the project with the name "Lfazen - ${staticProjectName}"
	And I go to the project with the name "Lfazen - ${staticProjectName}"
	And I go to the Attachments tab
	Then the attachment with the keyword "Document_2.txt" should be visible with the following values
	| Ticket                         | ${staticRequestId} |
	| File Name                      | Document_2.txt     |
	| File Name Link                 | true               |
	| File Size                      | 1KB                |
	| Attached                       | LFA Customer1      |
	| Does Not Contain Personal Data | false              |
	And the attachment with the keyword "Document_2.txt" should not have the actions or delete link visible

Scenario: View US data access file with no personal data as employees
	@ help.center.acceptance = "true"
	All employees in data access groups should be able to view links to large attachments with no personal data to a ticket uploaded by a customer in the US region

	Given I generate a provisioning project name
	And I create a user with the following parameters
	| Screen Name   | lfa.customer1                       |
	| Email Address | lfa.customer1@lrcustomer.com.broken |
	| First Name    | LFA                                 |
	| Last Name     | Customer1                           |
	And I create a user with the following parameters
	| Screen Name   | lfa.employee1                    |
	| Email Address | lfa.employee1@liferay.com.broken |
	| First Name    | LFA                              |
	| Last Name     | Employee1                        |
	| Group         | Employees                        |
	And I create a user with the following parameters
	| Screen Name   | lfa.employee2                    |
	| Email Address | lfa.employee2@liferay.com.broken |
	| First Name    | LFA                              |
	| Last Name     | Employee2                        |
	| Group         | Employees                        |
	And I create an account on koroneiki with the following values
	| Code        | LFAZENLFAZEN                  | |
	| Data Region | United States                 | |
	| Language    | English                       | |
	| Name        | Lfazen - ${staticProjectName} | |
	| Region      | United States                 | |
	| Status      | Active                        | |
	| Tier        | T1                            | |
	And I assign the contact with the email address "lfa.customer1@lrcustomer.com.broken" on the account "Lfazen - ${staticProjectName}" to the following roles
	| Support Requester |
	And I generate static start and end dates
	And I create a product purchase for an account with the name "Lfazen - ${staticProjectName}" and the product "Portal Production" on koroneiki with the following values
	| End Date                | ${staticEndDate}         |   |
	| Original End Date       | ${staticOriginalEndDate} |   |
	| Perpetual               | false                    |   |
	| Product Field and Value | sizing                   | 1 |
	| Product Field and Value | licenses                 | 1 |
	| Product Field and Value | version                  | 6 |
	| Quantity                | 1                        |   |
	| Start Date              | ${staticStartDate}       |   |
	| Status                  | Approved                 |   |
	And I create a product purchase for an account with the name "Lfazen - ${staticProjectName}" and the product "Gold Subscription" on koroneiki with the following values
	| End Date                | ${staticEndDate}         | |
	| Original End Date       | ${staticOriginalEndDate} | |
	| Perpetual               | false                    | |
	| Quantity                | 1                        | |
	| Start Date              | ${staticStartDate}       | |
	| Status                  | Approved                 | |
	And I synchronize the account entitlement definition with the name "Gold Subscription"
	And I synchronize the contact entitlement definition with the name "Customer"
	And I synchronize the contact entitlement definition with the name "Customer - DXP"
	And I synchronize the contact entitlement definition with the name "Customer - Portal"
	And I synchronize the contact entitlement definition with the name "Customer - Commerce"
	And I synchronize the contact entitlement definition with the name "Liferay Employee"
	And I wait for "1" minutes
	Then the support organization with the code "LFAZENLFAZEN" should be part of the support site
	And the organization "Lfazen - ${staticProjectName}" should be present on zendesk.liferay.com
	And the support user with the email address "lfa.customer1@lrcustomer.com.broken" should be synced to the support site
	And the support user with the email address "lfa.employee1@liferay.com.broken" should be synced to the support site
	And the support user with the email address "lfa.employee2@liferay.com.broken" should be synced to the support site
	And the user with the email address "lfa.customer1@lrcustomer.com.broken" should be present on zendesk.liferay.com
	And the user with the email address "lfa.employee1@liferay.com.broken" should be present on zendesk.liferay.com
	And the user with the email address "lfa.employee2@liferay.com.broken" should be present on zendesk.liferay.com
	When I update the support password for user with the email address "lfa.customer1@lrcustomer.com.broken" to "${staticSupportUserTestPassword}"
	And I update the support password for user with the email address "lfa.employee1@liferay.com.broken" to "${staticSupportUserTestPassword}"
	And I update the support password for user with the email address "lfa.employee2@liferay.com.broken" to "${staticSupportUserTestPassword}"
	And I assign the support user with the email address "lfa.employee1@liferay.com.broken" to the support organization "Data Access US"
	And I assign the support user with the email address "lfa.employee2@liferay.com.broken" to the support organization "Data Access EU"
	When I update the user with the email address "lfa.customer1@lrcustomer.com.broken" to use the password "zendeskqauser"
	And I log out and log into the support homepage as "lfa.customer1@lrcustomer.com.broken" with password "${staticSupportUserTestPassword}"
	And I log into zendesk as "lfa.customer1@lrcustomer.com.broken" with password "zendeskqauser"
	And I create a request with the following values
	| Product       | Liferay Portal                          | 6.2                                   |
	| Component     | Activation Key & Project Administration |                                       |
	| System Status | Production                              | Functioning with limited capabilities |
	| Subject       | Request Subject                         |                                       |
	| Description   | Request Description                     |                                       |
	| Attachments   | Document_1.txt                          |                                       |
	Then I should be able to view a request with the following details
	| Subject       | Request Subject                                    |
	| Status        | OPEN                                               |
	| Requester     | LFA Customer1                                      |
	| Priority      | Normal                                             |
	| Product       | Liferay Portal > 6.2                               |
	| Sub-Status    | —                                                  |
	| Component     | Activation Key & Project Administration            |
	| System Status | Production > Functioning with limited capabilities |
	| Attachments   | Document_1.txt                                     |
	And I upload a file using the large file uploader with the following parameters
	| Attachment       | Document_2.txt      |
	| Comment          | Large File Comment  |
	| Data Region      | United States       |
	| No Personal Data | true                |
	Then I should be able to view a large file comment containing the text "Large File Comment" with the following details
	| Author      | LFA Customer1      |
	| Comment     | Large File Comment |
	| Attachment  | Document_2.txt     |
	When I log out and log into the support homepage as "lfa.employee1@liferay.com.broken" with password "${staticSupportUserTestPassword}"
	And I go to the Project Details page
	And I search for the project with the name "Lfazen - ${staticProjectName}"
	And I go to the project with the name "Lfazen - ${staticProjectName}"
	And I go to the Attachments tab
	Then the attachment with the keyword "Document_2.txt" should be visible with the following values
	| Ticket                         | ${staticRequestId} |
	| File Name                      | Document_2.txt     |
	| File Name Link                 | true               |
	| File Size                      | 1KB                |
	| Attached                       | LFA Customer1      |
	| Does Not Contain Personal Data | true               |
	And the attachment with the keyword "Document_2.txt" should not have the actions or delete link visible
	When I log out and log into the support homepage as "lfa.employee2@liferay.com.broken" with password "${staticSupportUserTestPassword}"
	And I go to the Project Details page
	And I search for the project with the name "Lfazen - ${staticProjectName}"
	And I go to the project with the name "Lfazen - ${staticProjectName}"
	And I go to the Attachments tab
	Then the attachment with the keyword "Document_2.txt" should be visible with the following values
	| Ticket                         | ${staticRequestId} |
	| File Name                      | Document_2.txt     |
	| File Name Link                 | true               |
	| File Size                      | 1KB                |
	| Attached                       | LFA Customer1      |
	| Does Not Contain Personal Data | true               |
	And the attachment with the keyword "Document_2.txt" should not have the actions or delete link visible

